type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

!! Overview

Replaces the flat tiddler list in the "Contents" tab of the plugin info panel with up to two hierarchical tree views, grouped by `/`-separated path segments — the same style of tree used elsewhere in TiddlyWiki (e.g. tag trees).

Not every tiddler bundled in a plugin is named after it. A plugin can also ship:

* tiddlers named ''under its own title'' (`<plugin-title>/modules/foo`, `<plugin-title>/language/en-GB/`, …)
* shadow tiddlers ''outside its own title'' — overrides of a core or third-party tiddler (this very plugin does exactly that with `$:/core/ui/PluginInfo/Default/contents`) or arbitrary global tiddlers (a new `$:/tags/…` entry, a standalone `$:/config/…`, …)

The Contents tab now shows a top-level `!` heading (''Shadows shipped in the plugin''), then one tree per group, each with a `!!` heading and only rendered when non-empty:

# ''Namespace tiddlers'' — tiddlers nested under `<plugin-title>/`
# ''Other'' — everything else the plugin ships, outside its own title

A folder whose only direct child is a single sub-folder is shown on one line (`themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/`).

!! How it works

This plugin overrides a single shadow tiddler: `$:/core/ui/PluginInfo/Default/contents`. It splits `plugintiddlers[]` (the full list of tiddlers bundled in the plugin, regardless of naming) on the title prefix, then renders each group with a small local `nk-tree` macro (defined in `macros/tree.tid`) — a copy of the core `tree` macro's recursive branch/leaf logic, generalised to walk an arbitrary title list (via `enlist`) instead of the hardcoded `all[shadows+tiddlers]`. The macro also collapses single-child folder chains.

⚠️ Because this is a shadow tiddler override, it is ''global'': once installed, it changes the Contents tab for ''every'' plugin's info panel in the wiki — not just for this plugin.

!! Requirements

TiddlyWiki >= 5.2.0. No other dependency — it only relies on the `tree` macro shipped with the TiddlyWiki core.

